   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">FSC-R1: Shortterm livelihood support</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Activities within Oromia region: Distribute drought resistant and locally adaptable small ruminants to restore critical livelihoods assets of 120 households (5 shoats per HH),Provide selected drought resiting seed to 200 hh, Provide capacity building trainings for 28 Rural SACCOs (RuSACCO) executive committes on fund management, Support 4 RuSACCOs with different office supplies. Provide different need based farm tools to 500HHs; Provide seed money to 75 youth and 50 caregivers to engage on feasible IGA                                                                                                     Activities within Amhara region:  Rehabilitate 100 damaged shops and shades run by young IGA promotors.    Support 100 IGA propotors through business developemnt training, advocacy with financial institutions that have given them micro credits for extened payment periods. Support the rehabilitation of 100 residential houses burnt during conflict. provision of improved seeds, agrcicultural tools and fertilizers to 800 HHS. Provision of small ruminants to 150 HHs. Support the establishment of 600 VSLAs ( Village saving and lending associations)and 10 SHGs   (Self Help groups).    Six rounds of conditional cash transfer for OVC and persons with disability   Cash for work program for 300 HHs  for three months</narrative>
   </description>
